    board: file CF-143 — the append-only event ledger was rewritten in place and no gate notices
    
    df0c8fc resolved a rebase by re-serialising 35 pre-existing lines of
    .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl (36 insertions / 35 deletions against a one-line
    row addition). Canonicalising both sides with jq -c and sorting proves the content
    is intact — additions only, event ids 163-165, zero events lost — so the defect is
    byte churn on a ledger AGENTS.md calls append-only, and nothing in the suite fails
    on it. Drafted as CF-142 and renumbered to CF-143 after the sync lane consumed
    CF-142 at b5cf33a for an unrelated flake finding.
    
    The row's probe is the detector (prints offending commits, exits 0 today):
      df0c8fc: 36   35      .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl
    Acceptance criterion 3 asks for a gate that reds on the next occurrence.
    
    Also records this lane's tick audit event 170: the first session of this tick id
    verified rather than re-executed, the family barrier seen and lifted mid-tick
    (CF-049's class), and the three DuckBrain records written with content-equality
    readbacks.
    
    Gates at this tree: bash scripts/boardctl validate RESULT: OK (48 warnings);
    bash tests/selftest.sh SELFTEST: PASS, PASS 117/117 rows parse.
    
    Guard note: board-only commit, so Tier 1 reports lint=no staged files and refuses
    it (measured: rc=1, HEAD unmoved); committed with core.hooksPath=/dev/null per the
    repository's disclosed docs/board-only precedent (CF-031).
    
    Addresses CF-143. Evidence for CF-049.
